  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Angolans carry Portuguese first names (João, Domingos, Esperança, Domingas) or modern ones that are very Angolan (Adilson, Edvaldo, Délcio, Yolanda, Jandira), and often two surnames. Surnames are Portuguese (dos Santos, da Silva, Neto, Gonçalves), surnames that come from a forebear's first name (Domingos, Sebastião, Francisco, Pascoal), or African surnames from the family's community: Kimbundu ones around Luanda and Malanje, Umbundu ones from the central highlands (Huambo, Bié, Benguela), and Kikongo ones from the north (Uíge, Zaire). African first names are given too, often with meaning: Nzola (love) and Kiesse (joy) in Kikongo, Tchissola (love) in Umbundu, Nzinga after the seventeenth century queen. Older people are called Kota or Mais-velho as a mark of respect.",
